WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.900
- So, former officer Derek Chauvin

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.470
has been remanded into custody.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.390
He is now in jail.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.860
Eventually, he will appeal his case.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:07.693
This was always a case

00:00:07.693 --> 00:00:09.250
where if Chauvin was
convicted of anything,

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.520
it was clear that he was going to appeal.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.330
Generally speaking, criminal appeals

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.930
have a very, very low rate

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.270
of actually changing the outcome at trial.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.900
It can happen, but it's pretty rare.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.530
But one thing that will
definitely not happen

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.920
is this case will not go before

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.100
the United States Supreme Court.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.550
People will talk about taking things

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.460
all the way to the Supreme
court all the time,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.490
but the Supreme Court
doesn't really intervene,

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.710
number one, in state cases that much.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.960
And number two, they
don't really intervene

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.430
when it's just an application
of facts to the law.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.210
All of the legal standards
that were at issue

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.300
in the Chauvin trial are
pretty well cut and dry,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.790
so there's nothing for the US
Supreme Court to intervene on.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.550
It's possible that the
Minnesota Supreme Court

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.230
might weigh in on the murder 3
charge that was brought here,

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.850
but that's not likely to
have much of an effect

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.160
because Chauvin was convicted of murder 2.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.880
So, while you might be
seeing this in court,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.480
you will not be seeing this
in the US Supreme Court.

